From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lef <me@lefteros.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:45:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-husky: give the framebuffer
 a panel size

The framebuffer node has no panel, so simpledrm estimates the display's
physical size from its pixels at 96 dpi. On the 1344x2992 panel that is
355x791 mm instead of about 70x155 mm. Hyprland reports it, and
squeekboard sizes the on-screen keyboard with it: 105 of 935 logical
pixels (11% of the screen) instead of 196 (21%) with the real size.

Add a panel node at the root with width-mm and height-mm and point the
framebuffer at it. The node is disabled and not under /chosen, whose
schema only allows framebuffer and pinctrl children. The
simple-framebuffer binding has simpledrm read the size from the node it
points to, but with an enabled node without a driver fw_devlink makes the
framebuffer wait for ever (no DRM device appears and the screen stays on
the boot logo), and booting with fw_devlink=permissive instead takes
away the ordering that acpm-protocol needs after exynos-mailbox (16
channels, 0 usable, so no PMIC and no touch). of_link_to_phandle()
creates no link to a supplier that has no device and is not available,
and simpledrm reads the two properties without looking at the status.

70x155 mm is Google's own value for this panel: HK3_WIDTH_MM and
HK3_HEIGHT_MM in panel-gs-hk3.c (kernel/devices/google/shusky).

Tested on a Pixel 8 Pro (Kioxia UFS 4.0) on the husky-test-20261031-c6
kernel with the same node and property added by a device tree overlay:
simpledrm initialises, acpm-protocol reports 16 channels, 16 usable,
salixp binds, Hyprland reports 70x155 mm and the keyboard layer is
196 px tall. The commit as it stands (the node at the root) builds
and adds no dtbs_check error for the node; it has not been booted as
a built-in node.

Signed-off-by: Lef <me@lefteros.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
index 29b9a11b9..441c3a3c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-husky.dts
@@ -46,6 +46,22 @@ ufs_0_fixed_vcc_reg: regulator-ufs-vcc {
 		enable-active-high;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Without a panel node simpledrm estimates the display's physical
+	 * size from its pixels at 96 dpi: 355x791 mm instead of 70x155 mm,
+	 * which sizes everything that works in millimetres (the on-screen
+	 * keyboard is half as tall as it should be) wrongly. simpledrm only
+	 * reads width-mm and height-mm from this node. It stays disabled so
+	 * that fw_devlink does not make the framebuffer wait for a driver
+	 * this node will never have. 70x155 mm is HK3_WIDTH_MM and
+	 * HK3_HEIGHT_MM in Google's panel-gs-hk3.c for the Pixel 8 Pro.
+	 */
+	panel0: panel {
+		status = "disabled";
+		width-mm = <70>;
+		height-mm = <155>;
+	};
+
 	chosen {
 		/*
 		 * ABL requires bootargs to exist; it appends its own after these.
@@ -70,6 +86,7 @@ chosen {
 		 */
 		framebuffer0: framebuffer {
 			compatible = "simple-framebuffer";
+			panel = <&panel0>;
 			memory-region = <&cont_splash_mem>;
 			width = <1344>;
 			height = <2992>;
